        },
        {
          "id": 805120619,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I thought about it, but I'm a little unsure about whether actually generated pcaps technically count as \"documentation\" for purposes of the RFC, and ULAs are definitely fine. (Somewhat related discussion: https://networkengineering.stackexchange.com/questions/44121/where-can-i-use-the-ipv6-documentation-prefix).\n\nThat does remind me that we certainly *should* use those for the [documentation](doc/text2pcap.adoc) and [examples](text2pcap.c#L238-240), which right now use link local addresses from `fe80::/10`",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-09T17:14:23.003Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-09T17:14:23.003Z",
